[{"id":2934902418,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6u7w6S","user":{"login":"lyuma","id":39946030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5OTQ2MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39946030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma","html_url":"https://github.com/lyuma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lyuma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"So if I understand, the issue is that wav uses *unsigned* uint32, while Godot integers are signed when exposed in APIs (or when used in vectors). I think it makes sense....\r\n\r\nA lot of my uncertainty comes down also to code style. For example, given that Vector.resize() returns an Error, is it better to store that in a variable, and then call `ERR_FAIL_COND_V(err, ...)` , or better to do it on one line as this code is written.\r\n\r\nI would like @AThousandShips to take a look at this code and see if it's going in the right direction in terms of code quality + style. If she thinks it is good, and there's some way to verify that this fixes an issue (MRP / example case) then I think I'd be okay approving this change.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107596#pullrequestreview-2934902418","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107596","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107596#pull